Bound the memory spike of prompt_logprobs (fork).

The V2 runner computes prompt logprobs in chunks of 1024 prompt tokens. Each
chunk's logits span the whole vocabulary (248,320 for Qwen3.8) and the
top-k/log-softmax temporaries come on top -- more than 1 GiB that the startup
memory profile never sees. On 2x RTX 3090 at TP=2 with the KV pool sized to
GPU_UTIL 0.93, quality_battery.py's perplexity requests raised
torch.OutOfMemoryError in compute_logits and the worker took the whole engine
down (EngineDeadError) -- any client asking for prompt_logprobs could do that.

VLLM_PROMPT_LOGPROBS_CHUNK sets the chunk (default 1024 as upstream); the
launchers set 128. The result is identical, the loop just runs more often:
after the change the same battery runs against the same server (PPL 8.569 as
before) and 8k / 30k-token prompts with prompt_logprobs=1 return in 3.6 / 14.5 s.

--- fork: hand-written against the installed series (0.30.0 + every patch above it in patches/series) ---
